# "You may play lands from your graveyard" uses the turn's land play (CR 305.2) and offers nothing but lands, and only
# the Crucible's controller's. Bot1 bolts Bot2 (Lightning Bolt in the graveyard is not castable), cracks Marsh Flats
# and casts Crucible with Black Lotus. On turn 3 it plays an Island from hand and so may not replay the Flats from the
# graveyard; on turn 5 it does. Bot2 has no Crucible and may not play its own cracked Marsh Flats from its graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Marsh Flats
Black Lotus
Crucible of Worlds
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island
Island
Swamp
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Marsh Flats
Island x7
Swamp
Island x6

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Marsh Flats.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Marsh Flats.Activate
Bot1.Search(Swamp)
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Crucible of Worlds.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Marsh Flats.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Marsh Flats.Activate
Bot2.Search(Swamp)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
! Bot1.Graveyard.Marsh Flats.Play
! Bot1.Graveyard.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot2.Graveyard.Marsh Flats.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Graveyard.Marsh Flats.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.LandsPlayed = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Island; Marsh Flats; Mox Ruby; Crucible of Worlds
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus; Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Graveyard = Island; Marsh Flats
